    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="0736" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/2608: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Colonel E. M. House
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-05T19:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 5, 1918—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. [From President Wilson.] Please let Mr. Hoover know that, very much to my
                    regret, I fear that the terms of the appropriation for National Security and
                    Defence would not justify my making the allotment to which he refers. Woodrow
                        Wilson.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d537-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d537-f1" n="22" xml:id="d537-f1-content">
                <p>See Colonel House’s telegram No. 214, Dec. 1, 1918, 10 p.m., <ref target="#pg645"
                        >p. 645</ref>.</p>
